attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 2, `gmk` to `yicG`, are carried by 92 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 2% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 93 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 1, `ligB`, 93% {S1}.

@variable **A variable column follows**, column 3, `dinD`, carried by 78% {S2.c3}. The fork at columns 19 to 24, [[lipopolysaccharide core]], is carried by 36 to 55%, the most plastic stretch of the window, in a region of plasticity in 63 to 93% of calls {S6, P, Q}. A second branch of 5 families runs through columns 19 to 23, a parallel path carried instead of the most carried families there, share 19% {S6.b19}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 90 against 82%, and hesitates less there, 0.28 against 0.32 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 52, `yibG`, is a variable column, at 1.00 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends in fork columns.** Columns 56 to 79 are carried by 1 to 88% of chromosomes, 15 shell and 9 persistent {S12}. The last column is `xylG`, in 43% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 87% of genes**, 0.30 bits on average, perplexity 1.7 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.59 against 0.17 bits, and names fewer genes, 73% against 93% {C}.

